# The pedal workspace

This directory is the workspace root: the directory an agent session is opened on, and the root
the file sandbox grants. Everything the pedal is made of is inside it, which is what makes working
across the repositories ordinary rather than a series of permission requests.

It is deliberately **not a git repository**, and must never become one. The six repositories
below are independent, and a repository here could only record them as gitlinks — pointers to
commits that clone as empty directories. There is nothing to commit at this level, so there is
nothing to get wrong; `git init` here is the one mistake with no upside.

Whichever harness you are using: open **this** folder, not a repository inside it. A session
opened on `namchain/` can read its siblings but cannot write them.

## What is here

| Directory | What it is |
|---|---|
| `pedal.project/` | The pedal as a system: goal, hardware design, diagrams, decisions, plan, the Core host's configuration as code, the Pico firmware and `pedald` |
| `namchain/` | The engine: the `namchaind` library and daemon, `namchainctl`, the control protocol, the soak and bench tools |
| `namchain/vendor/NeuralAmpModelerCore/` | The planar-NEON fork of NeuralAmpModelerCore, vendored as a **declared submodule** on `all-optimisations` |
| `ljoss/` | The rig designer (macOS/iOS) and the front end that drives the engine |
| `rtpi/` | The Core host's PREEMPT_RT kernel, its boot-slot safety net, and device-tree work |
| `NAMBench/` | NAM and IR kernel research; it reaches the pedal through `namchain` |
| `rigpa/` | The pedal's on-device UI (C++, Qt 6): runs on the Core host, talks to `namchaind` and `pedald` |

`.worktrees/` holds per-session git worktrees, when two agents need one repository at once. It is
hidden, so ripgrep skips it.

## Before you do anything

Read `pedal.project/AGENTS.md`. It is canonical for the whole project — the hardware constraints,
the commands, the working rules — and `pedal.project/docs/working-across-repos.md` says which
repository owns what and how a change reaches the pedal.

**Work in the repository that owns the change.** Each repository's own `AGENTS.md` is
authoritative inside that repository; this file only says where they are.

Start a session with `pedal.project/scripts/status`, which reports every checkout, the Core host's
lock and what it is running. `pedal.project/scripts/workspace check` asserts the layout, the root
files and the git guard.

## The one rule about git here

A repository may be inside another repository **only when it is declared** — `git submodule add`,
which records the URL and pins the commit in `.gitmodules`. A checkout dropped into a tracked
directory is the accident that clones as an empty directory and never says so, and it is refused
by a hook (`pedal.project/tools/git-hooks/`) rather than left to be remembered. If a tool fetches
dependencies into a repository, that path belongs in the repository's `.gitignore` and its fetch
script owns it.

`pedal.project/docs/workspace.md` is the design: why this shape, what `scripts/workspace` does,
and what everything here is checked against.
